<h2>Cookie Policy</h2>

<p>This Cookie Policy explains how we use cookies on our website in accordance 
with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the ePrivacy Directive.</p>

<h3>1. What are cookies?</h3>
<p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device. They help websites operate, 
improve performance, and deliver personalized content.</p>

<h3>2. Types of cookies we use</h3>

<h4>Essential Cookies</h4>
<p>Required for the site to work (session, security, load balancing). These do not 
require consent under EU law.</p>

<h4>Analytics Cookies</h4>
<p>Used to understand website usage and improve the user experience. Set only if 
you give consent.</p>

<h4>Marketing Cookies</h4>
<p>Used for advertising and tracking across websites. Set only if you give consent.</p>

<h3>3. Managing your cookie preferences</h3>
<p>You can update your cookie choices at any time using the “Cookie Settings” link 
available on every page.</p>

<h3>4. Legal basis</h3>
<p>Essential cookies are processed under legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).  
Analytics and marketing cookies require your prior consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>

<h3>5. How long cookies are stored</h3>
<p>Storage times vary depending on cookie type and purpose. Most cookies expire 
between 1 day and 2 years.</p>

<h3>6. Contact</h3>
<p>If you have questions about our use of cookies, contact:  
<strong>support@lonelypartner.com</strong></p>

